You have an internal hordeolum, which is a stye inside the eyelid. It happens when one of the oil glands within the eyelid becomes blocked and infected.\
\
This usually causes localized tenderness, swelling, and redness. Sometimes it drains and settles on its own, and sometimes it leaves behind a painless, firm lump called a chalazion which may benefit from further treatment. \
\
